MODIFIED — not a verbatim copy. Changes from upstream, all confined to
SKILL.md and reviewable as a diff against the pinned commit above:
  1. frontmatter `description` rewritten: removed the proactive auto-fire
     clause and the bare "get a second opinion" trigger (which collided
     with the codex-server skill), narrowed activation to explicit user
     requests on high-stakes questions, and added a cost statement plus a
     go-ahead gate before launching a panel.
  2. appended a `## Local interop notes` section routing the tier-1
     external-family panelist to codex-server/codex-cli, recording the
     600000 ms Bash timeout ceiling, and preferring the Workflow tool.
The 162-line protocol body between the frontmatter and that section is
byte-for-byte identical to upstream.

